[?2004l[?2004h>     "a0576a26f2a2eeac": {
[?2004l[?2004h>         "answer": "The recommended dosage of lopinavir and ritonavir oral solution in adults is either 800 mg/200 mg (10 mL) once daily, or 400 mg/100 mg (5 mL) twice daily. The dose must be increased to 520 mg/130 mg (6.5 mL) twice daily when administered in combination with efavirenz, nevirapine, or nelfinavir. Once daily dosing is not recommended in pediatric patients, pregnant women, or in combination with carbamazepine, phenobarbital, phenytoin, efavirenz, nevirapine, or nelfinavir, or in patients with three or more lopinavir resistance-associated substitutions.",
