[?2004l[?2004h>         "answer": "The safety risks of lopinavir and ritonavir include serious adverse reactions due to drug interactions (as a CYP3A inhibitor), toxicity in preterm neonates (due to ethanol and propylene glycol content), pancreatitis (which can be fatal), hepatotoxicity (especially in patients with hepatitis B or C), QT and PR interval prolongation (which can lead to atrioventricular block), diabetes mellitus/hyperglycemia, immune reconstitution syndrome, lipid elevations (large increases in cholesterol and triglycerides), fat redistribution, increased bleeding in patients with hemophilia, and resistance/cross-resistance. Commonly reported adverse reactions in adults include diarrhea (reported by at least half of patients on once-daily dosing), nausea, vomiting, hypertriglyceridemia, and hypercholesterolemia.",
